1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Nightingale brings a shared care record
into one clear workspace for this team.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
I begin as Staff with Sarah Tan, then wait
for the workspace to settle.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,000
The page clearly separates notes,
suggestions, actions, and review history.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The team can see what needs attention
and why right now for everyone.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Staff starts with Glance View, where key
items are visible together at once.

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Each card shows content, a next step,
review status, item kind, risk, priority.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Priority organises the view; it is not a
medical risk score to guide review.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,000
I open the original source of an
AI-assisted note for careful team review.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:56,000
The page takes me smoothly to the matching
timeline entry for team verification.

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,000
The highlighted passage stays tied to its
original record version in context.

11
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:10,000
The evidence is easy to inspect; closing
Source leaves the record unchanged.

12
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Here is a Voice note: a pre-recorded
synthetic care conversation with audio.

13
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:23,000
I follow the prepared timestamped
transcript at every step for clear timing.

14
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Each segment connects to a reviewable
care-note suggestion for the care team.

15
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:38,000
I select a segment, open its source, and
keep the exact highlighted path.

16
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:47,000
The suggestion is ready for clinician
review today and supports safe follow-up.

17
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Back in Staff, I edit the existing Staff
note and save a new revision for review.

18
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:59,000
I wait for the saved state before
continuing with patient care.

19
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Then I add a team discussion and mention
Clinician A from the visible menu.

20
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:15,000
The discussion stays with the record;
staff can follow up in context.

21
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Resolve and Unresolve make discussion
status explicit for the whole team.

22
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:34,000
I assign this follow-up to Clinician A
with clear ownership in this workflow.

23
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:45,000
The task becomes active immediately;
Open status and ownership show in Glance.

24
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Now I switch to Clinician, and I open
the assigned task for review in context.

25
00:02:52,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Assigned tasks become active immediately
and move through Open, In progress, and Done.

26
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:08,000
I edit the Clinician plan, save, and open
History for careful team review.

27
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:17,000
I compare an earlier version with the
current one before reviewing the change.

28
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:24,000
Before and After show the change; Revert
creates a version and preserves history.

29
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:33,000
I accept one AI suggestion; it becomes
Reviewed, and its source stays unchanged.

30
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:42,000
I reject another AI suggestion; it leaves
active Glance; its source remains.

31
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Historical context brings recent and
earlier summaries together for review.

32
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:56,000
Each summary is labelled clearly and links
to original records for team verification.

33
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:03,000
I open an original record and reach the
relevant timeline point when needed.

34
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:10,000
An independent participant used Simplified
Chinese; the glance task had no coaching.

35
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:16,000
The result was approximately nine seconds,
with all four observations correct.

36
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Finally, I switch to Patient; the patient
view contains only shared information.

37
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:28,000
It shows care summaries, instructions, and
patient conversation.

38
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Internal items, team discussions, tasks,
and clinician-only controls stay out.

39
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Patient Voice follows this path: audio,
timestamped transcript, and care context.

40
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Next steps stay visible; the original
record stays verifiable for everyone.

41
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Human review remains at every suggestion
boundary in this workflow.

42
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:55,000
The demo uses synthetic data and a hosted
HTTPS workspace for a traceable workflow.
